doc:administrative_action_aliens_office_refusal_2016_09_13 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "refusal to grant “humanitarian visas” by the Aliens Office"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensOffice ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 September 2016 the Aliens Office, the administrative body responsible for issuing visas (see paragraph 45 below), refused to grant “humanitarian visas” to the applicants and informed them of its decisions by an email of 29 September 2016, transmitted through the visa department of the Belgian embassy in Beirut."^^xsd:string,
        "The court of appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016 was thus no longer operative, given that the Aliens Office’s refusal decisions of 13 September 2016 had become final and irrevocable before the penalty payment was issued against the Belgian State."^^xsd:string .

doc:administrative_action_aliens_office_refusal_2016_10_10 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Office’s decisions of 10 October 2016"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensOffice ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the Aliens Office’s decisions of 10 October 2016"^^xsd:string .

doc:belgianEmbassyBeirut a echr:DomesticAuthority ;
    rdfs:label "Belgian embassy in Beirut"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityAdministrative ;
    echr:hasJurisdictionState "Belgium"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 22 August 2016 the applicant couple, accompanied by one of their children, travelled to the Belgian embassy in Beirut to submit visa applications for themselves and their two children."^^xsd:string .

doc:case_3599_18 a echr:CaseDocument ;
    rdfs:label "Application no. 3599/18 M.N. and Others against Belgium"@en ;
    echr:hasApplicant doc:partyTheApplicants ;
    echr:hasApplicationNumber "3599/18"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasDomesticProceeding doc:domestic_proceeding_admin_challenge_aliens_office_2016,
        doc:domestic_proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_set_aside_2017_03_24,
        doc:domestic_proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_stay_2016_10_20,
        doc:domestic_proceeding_conseil_detat_appeal_2018_05_17 ;
    echr:hasExtractionNote "No domestic proceedings described in the provided excerpt: the procedural paragraphs instead record the Strasbourg allocation, relinquishment to the Grand Chamber and hearing dates."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasRespondentState "Belgium"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "The applicants complained that the Belgian authorities’ refusal to issue them with the so-called “humanitarian” visas had exposed them to a situation incompatible with Article 3 of the Convention (prohibition of torture and of inhuman or degrading treatment) with no possibility of remedying it effectively, as required by Article 13 (right to an effective remedy)."^^xsd:string,
        "The applicants further alleged a violation of Article 6 § 1 (right to a fair hearing) and Article 13 of the Convention, in that it was impossible for them to pursue the execution of the Brussels Court of Appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016 ordering the Belgian State to execute the Aliens Appeals Board’s judgment of 20 October 2016, which had instructed the Belgian authorities to issue them with the visas they had requested under Article 3 of the Convention."^^xsd:string,
        "The case originated in an application (no. 3599/18) against Belgium lodged with the Court under Article 34 of the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms (“the Convention”) on 10 January 2018 by a married couple and their two minor children, all Syrian nationals (“the applicants”)."^^xsd:string .

doc:domestic_proceeding_brussels_court_of_appeal_2016_12_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal judgment varying order of 7 November 2016 (7 December 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:domestic_proceeding_tpi_inter_partes_2016_11_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeClaimGranted ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionFavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_brussels_appeal_2016_12_07,
        doc:participation_belgian_state_brussels_appeal_2016_12_07 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On an appeal by the applicants, the Brussels Court of Appeal delivered a judgment on 7 December 2016 varying the order of 7 November 2016. It held that the applicants could rely on the binding and enforceable nature of the contested judgment and on their subjective right to seek compliance and obtain an end to the harm sustained by them as a result of non-execution of the judgment, which constituted “an illegal action” and manifest fault."^^xsd:string,
        "The court of appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016 was thus no longer operative, given that the Aliens Office’s refusal decisions of 13 September 2016 had become final and irrevocable before the penalty payment was issued against the Belgian State."^^xsd:string .

doc:domestic_proceeding_brussels_court_of_appeal_2016_12_14 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal judgment (14 December 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:domestic_proceeding_tpi_unilateral_2016_12_13 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12-14"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeOther ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionUnfavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_brussels_appeal_2016_12_14,
        doc:participation_belgian_state_brussels_appeal_2016_12_14 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "However, on an appeal by the Belgian State, the court of appeal varied the decision of the first-instance court in a judgment of 14 December 2016. It noted the Belgian State’s intention to raise the difficulties of complying with the judgment of 7 December 2016 with the enforcement judge (“ le juge des saisies ”) and ordered the applicants not to pursue further enforcement proceedings pending a decision by the enforcement judge who was to rule on the validity of the enforcement procedure and the State’s right to restrict the amounts due in respect of penalty payments."^^xsd:string .

doc:domestic_proceeding_brussels_court_of_appeal_2017_06_30 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal judgment (30 June 2017)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:domestic_proceeding_aliens_appeals_board_set_aside_2017_03_24 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-06-30"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionUnfavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_brussels_appeal_2017_06_30,
        doc:participation_belgian_state_brussels_appeal_2017_06_30 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "For its part, the Belgian State sought to counter the execution of the above-cited decisions; it secured this aim through the court of appeal’s judgment of 30 June 2017."^^xsd:string,
        "The applicants did not appeal on points of law against the Brussels Court of Appeal’s judgment of 30 June 2017, on the grounds that the lawyer at the Court of Cassation assigned to their case by the Legal Aid Board had informed them such an appeal would have no reasonable prospect of success."^^xsd:string .

doc:domestic_proceeding_enforcement_judge_decision_2017_12_20 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement judge decision (20 December 2017)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:domestic_proceeding_enforcement_judge_applicants_2016_12_15 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:enforcementJudgeBrussels ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-12-20"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeDiscontinued ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionUnfavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_enforcement_2017_12_20 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 20 December 2017 the French-language enforcement judge, examining the action brought by the applicants on 15 December 2016, found that the case had become devoid of purpose following the Brussels Court of Appeal’s judgment of 30 June 2017."^^xsd:string .

doc:domestic_proceeding_enforcement_judge_state_2016_12_15 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "proceedings before the enforcement judge at the Brussels Dutch‐language TPI (15 December 2016)"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsTpiDutch ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_enforcement_2016_12_15_bis,
        doc:participation_belgian_state_enforcement_2016_12_15 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2016-12-15"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On the same date the Belgian State brought proceedings against the applicants before the enforcement judge at the Brussels Dutch ‐ language TPI, seeking a stay of execution of the principal sentence ... and/or to prevent other enforcement measures, such as penalty payments."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:isPending true .

doc:domestic_proceeding_state_points_of_law_2017_02_27 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "appeal on points of law by the Belgian State (27 February 2017)"@en ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_belgian_state_points_of_law_2017_02_27 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2017-02-27"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 27 February 2017 the Belgian State lodged an appeal on points of law against the court of appeal’s judgment of 7 December 2016. Those proceedings are currently pending."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:isPending true .

doc:domestic_proceeding_tpi_unilateral_2016_10_25 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "unilateral application before the President of the Brussels French-language Court of First Instance (order of 25 October 2016)"@en ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsTpi ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelFirstInstance ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeMeasureImposed ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionFavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_tpi_2016_10_25,
        doc:participation_belgian_state_tpi_2016_10_25 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By an order of 25 October 2016, considering that the failure by the Aliens Office to comply with a judgment of the Aliens Appeals Board, notwithstanding the fact that it had been immediately enforceable, constituted “an unacceptable illegal action”, the acting president of the French-language TPI ordered the State, as an urgent measure, to comply with the Board’s judgment of 20 October 2016, that is, to issue the applicants with visas or laissez-passers , and made the order subject to a penalty payment of 1,000 euros (EUR) per day of delay and per applicant."^^xsd:string .

doc:enforcement_action_payment_order_2016_12_13 a echr:EnforcementAction ;
    rdfs:label "payment order in respect of the penalties (13 December 2016)"@en ;
